<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lugal-Anne-mundu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lugal-Anne-mundu was a king of Adab in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumer">Sumer</a> and the only ruler of that city named in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list">Sumerian King List</a>, which credits him with a reign of 90 years. Old Babylonian copies of inscriptions attributed to him claim conquests from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>. No contemporary records confirm these claims, and his date, probably in the mid-3rd millennium BCE, is uncertain.</p></div>
